# Normalise line endings at the git layer, not per-developer machine.
#
# core.autocrlf=true rewrites LF blobs to CRLF in the Windows working tree.
# That is harmless for git, but it makes LF-only gates (.editorconfig, Prettier
# with endOfLine=lf) unable to pass locally - `prettier --check` reports every
# file as unformatted, forever, because writing the file immediately puts CRLF
# back. Committing the normalisation here makes the checkout match the blob on
# every platform, so the gates mean the same thing locally and in CI.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files must never be line-ending translated.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.whl binary
